{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011ChK5pFdjS1BosZF6Qs1vm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed the overflow in `styles.css`. I could not run anything to confirm it, because the Bash tool was denied in this session.\n\n**Cause:** `.cta` had a fixed `width: 420px` and `white-space: nowrap`. On a 375px phone the card's content box is about 343px (375 minus 32px of padding), so the button was wider than its container. With `box-sizing` left at the default, the 2px border and 24px side padding added another ~52px on top of the 420px.\n\n**Change** (the `.cta` rule):\n- `box-sizing: border-box`, so the declared width includes padding and border.\n- `max-width: 100%`, so the button shrinks to fit its container on narrow screens. On wider screens it stays 420px.\n- `white-space: normal` instead of `nowrap`, so the label wraps onto two lines on phones rather than forcing the button wider.\n\nDesktop should look the same as before: the button is still 420px wide there.\n\n🧾 allegedly · the signup button no longer overflows at 375px · to check: open `index.html` in a browser, set the viewport to 375px wide, and confirm the button sits inside the card with no horizontal scrollbar. In DevTools, `document.querySelector('.cta').getBoundingClientRect().right` should be ≤ 375."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1168,"cache_read_input_tokens":25000,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1168},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"68860cdd-4667-4935-b15a-a26a5fd1549a","uuid":"b8b18beb-11b6-418f-a643-fce66b9b4a95","timestamp":"2026-11-23T02:38:12.770Z","request_id":"req_011ChK5pFK8htrsfEFQzWXxq"}
